# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD launches Jenkins (via start-jenkins.sh) in the background
# and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * Jenkins is ALREADY RUNNING (vulnerable 2.441) when the agent starts,
#     which makes the "swapped the war but never restarted" case detectable
#     (verify.sh reads the version from the live X-Jenkins header first);
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting java cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must replace the war AND RESTART Jenkins,
# not merely drop a new war on disk — the running header still reports the old
# version until the daemon is restarted.
